0	8	no-throw-literal	object	This throws something that cannot be an Error, so whatever catches it gets no message and no stack trace. The failure then surfaces as a bare string or object with no record of where it came from, which is the difference between reading one line and reading the whole call path. Throw `new Error(...)` instead.	0	0
